From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:43:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shell: A prompt shows on the screen where the action was
 taken

With the desktop on a second screen (VNC) a PIN asked for by an app on
the desktop came up on the phone: a system modal without a monitor goes
to the primary one.

polkit names the process that asks. Its unit (dbus-:1.2-<app id>@.service
for an app activated through D-Bus, app-<launcher>-<app id>-<pid>.scope
for one started by GLib, Phosh or the desktop) gives the app, the app's
window gives the monitor: its active window, else its first window that
shows somewhere. Phosh's own requests (a quick setting on the phone)
stay on the primary monitor. Without such a window the monitor of the
active window is taken; while a layer surface of Phosh (the open top
panel, the lock screen) has the keyboard there is none, and the prompt
stays on the primary monitor.

The other prompts apps ask for, the keyring (gcr system prompt), network
secrets, app permissions (location, portals) and mount passwords, go to
the monitor of the active window. A window on two monitors counts for
the primary one. The end-session dialog and cell broadcasts stay on the
primary monitor.
